Hi there,

mapCountryData expects to have only one value per country. In your
case you have ten counts per country, that's not one value. So you
want to summarize the distribution. But you cannot ask for the "mean"
of a factor. Here we expect "Left" to be encoded by 1 and "Right" to
be encoded as 10, so it seems you took care of giving sound names to
the levels of your factor, and then we can go
"mean(as.numeric(wvs$v95))", or simply "mean(wvs$v95)", if I assume
that in your original data frame these are numerical values. And then
that's what you will give mapCountryData to plot, and the actual
crosstable is useless.

So from "wvs" or "wvsneu", you group by v2 and you summarize by the
mean of v95 before you give that to plot to mapCountryData. The
dataframe you give to mapCountryData should have exactly one row per
country.

With dplyr:
wvs %>% group_by(v2) %>% summarize(avg=mean(v95)) -> result
and then you will pass result to joinCountryData2Map and to
mapCountryData, with nameColumnToPlot="avg"

See for instance
http://stackoverflow.com/questions/2547402/standard-library-function-in-r-for-finding-the-mode
in case you want to plot the mode (most frequent value) instead of the
mean.

Good night,
   JB

